---
// What the reply changed, in the app's own labels. The comment is made only if it is confirmed.
const changes = [
	{ text: 'Moved "Store drop-off without a label" to another sprint' },
	{ text: 'Updated "Refund status emails": assignee' },
	{ text: 'Added a comment', comment: true },
];
const memories = [
	{ type: 'Decision', text: 'D-07: the return reason is optional.', source: 'Round 2 verdicts, topic "Return reasons"' },
	{ type: 'Decision', text: 'Customers look orders up by email or phone. The order number is optional.', source: 'Topic answered Oct 2' },
	{ type: 'Risk', text: 'Carrier API sandbox is down until Oct 20.', source: 'Raised by Marcus Chen' },
	{ type: 'Fact', text: 'Harbor & Pine support is open 8 to 6 Pacific, Monday to Saturday.', source: 'Brief, current state' },
	{ type: 'Outcome', text: 'Sprint 14 closed 3 points short. CSV export moved to Sprint 15.', source: 'Sprint 14 review' },
	{ type: 'Fact', text: 'Refunds go back to the original payment method.', source: 'Brief, proposed solution 4' },
];
---

<section class="section ravens" id="ai" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
	<div class="wrap section-head">
		<h2 id="ai-title">Thought and Memory.</h2>
		<p>
			In the old stories, Odin kept two ravens, Thought and Memory. Every day they flew over the world and came back
			with what they had seen. Odin's assistant has the same two jobs.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="wrap ravens__grid">
		<article class="raven">
			<header>
				<svg class="raven__rune" viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v30M28 5v30M12 14l16 12"></path></svg>
				<h3>Thought <span>Huginn</span></h3>
			</header>
			<p class="raven__lede">
				Ask the AI Workspace a question and it answers. If changes would help, it says what it would change and
				waits for your go-ahead. Tell it to do something and it does it in Odin, as you, with your permissions. It
				has 128 tools for plans, sprints, tickets, schedules, time, files, requirements and its own memory.
			</p>
			<div class="app thought" data-thought>
				<div class="thought__ask">
					<span class="a-av" style="--c:#7c4ddb">LP</span>
					<p>Sprint 15 is slipping. Move what you need to, and let Priya know.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="reply">
					<p class="a-small a-muted">Used 4 tools</p>
					<p>
						Sprint 15 is past halfway with 47% of points done. I moved "Store drop-off without a label" (8 pts) to
						Sprint 16 and gave "Refund status emails" to Sam, who has 6 free hours; Priya was 4 hours over. My comment
						for Priya mentions her, so Odin will email her.
					</p>
					<section class="confirm is-open" aria-label="Confirmation" data-confirm>
						<p class="confirm__title">
							<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M8 1 2.5 3v4.6c0 3.3 2.3 6.2 5.5 7.4 3.2-1.2 5.5-4.1 5.5-7.4V3L8 1Zm0 1.6 4 1.45V7.6c0 2.5-1.6 4.8-4 5.8-2.4-1-4-3.3-4-5.8V4.05l4-1.45ZM7.25 4.5v4h1.5v-4h-1.5Zm0 5v1.5h1.5V9.5h-1.5Z"></path></svg>
							Add a comment
						</p>
						<div class="confirm__actions" data-confirm-actions>
							<button type="button" class="a-btn a-btn--danger" data-answer="approve">Confirm</button>
							<button type="button" class="a-btn" data-answer="decline">Cancel</button>
						</div>
						<p class="a-small a-muted" data-confirm-outcome hidden></p>
					</section>
				</div>
				<div class="reply" data-done hidden>
					<p data-done-text></p>
					<section class="changes" aria-label="Changes in Odin">
						<div class="changes__head">
							<span data-changes-summary></span>
							<button type="button" class="changes__undo" data-undo>Undo</button>
						</div>
						<div class="changes__ask" role="group" aria-label="Undo these changes" data-undo-ask hidden>
							<p class="a-small" data-undo-question></p>
							<button type="button" class="a-btn a-btn--danger" data-undo-yes>Undo changes</button>
							<button type="button" class="a-btn" data-undo-no>Keep them</button>
						</div>
						<ul class="changes__list">
							{
								changes.map((change) => (
									<li data-change data-comment={change.comment ? '' : undefined}>
										<span>{change.text}</span>
										<span class="changes__state a-small">Undone</span>
									</li>
								))
							}
						</ul>
					</section>
				</div>
				<p class="thought__status a-small a-muted" data-thought-status aria-live="polite">
					The comment waits for you to confirm. The other two changes are already made.
				</p>
			</div>
			<ul class="raven__facts">
				<li>Deletes and anything that emails people wait for you to confirm</li>
				<li>Project-wide changes, such as sprints, dates and the brief, need a project admin or manager</li>
				<li>Undo reverses a reply's changes where it can, and leaves anything edited since</li>
			</ul>
		</article>

		<article class="raven">
			<header>
				<svg class="raven__rune" viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v30M28 5v30M12 6l16 14M28 6L12 20"></path></svg>
				<h3>Memory <span>Muninn</span></h3>
			</header>
			<p class="raven__lede">
				Odin keeps a short summary of every project, epic and story, and a memory of decisions, risks, outcomes and
				facts that it searches by meaning or keyword. People can add, correct and forget entries.
			</p>
			<div class="app memory" data-memory>
				<label class="memory__search">
					<span class="visually-hidden">Search what the AI remembers</span>
					<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M10.7 9.6a5.5 5.5 0 1 0-1.1 1.1l3.6 3.6 1.1-1.1-3.6-3.6ZM6.5 10.5a4 4 0 1 1 0-8 4 4 0 0 1 0 8Z"></path></svg>
					<input type="search" placeholder="Search what the AI remembers" data-memory-search />
				</label>
				<div class="memory__hints a-small">
					Try
					<button type="button" data-hint="return">return</button>
					<button type="button" data-hint="sprint">sprint</button>
					<button type="button" data-hint="carrier">carrier</button>
				</div>
				<ul class="memories" data-memory-list>
					{
						memories.map((memory) => (
							<li class="memory-row" data-memory-row>
								<span class:list={['a-chip', memory.type === 'Decision' ? 'a-chip--ok' : memory.type === 'Risk' ? 'a-chip--bad' : memory.type === 'Outcome' ? 'a-chip--merged' : 'a-chip--accent']}>{memory.type}</span>
								<div>
									<p>{memory.text}</p>
									<p class="a-small a-muted">{memory.source}</p>
								</div>
								<button type="button" class="a-btn forget" data-forget>
									Forget
								</button>
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ul>
				<p class="memory__empty a-small a-muted" data-memory-empty hidden>Nothing in memory matches that.</p>
			</div>
			<ul class="raven__facts">
				<li>Workspace admins set expiry and legal holds</li>
				<li>Each workspace can bring its own OpenAI key</li>
				<li>Admins pick the assistant's model, and the model and reasoning effort for eight AI helpers</li>
			</ul>
		</article>
	</div>
</section>

<script>
	// Thought: as in the AI Workspace, the comment that emails Priya waits for Confirm or Cancel.
	// Then the next reply lists what changed, with an Undo that asks once.
	const thought = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-thought]');
	if (thought) {
		const find = <T extends HTMLElement = HTMLElement>(selector: string) => thought.querySelector<T>(selector)!;
		const actions = find('[data-confirm-actions]');
		const outcome = find('[data-confirm-outcome]');
		const done = find('[data-done]');
		const doneText = find('[data-done-text]');
		const summary = find('[data-changes-summary]');
		const undo = find<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-undo]');
		const ask = find('[data-undo-ask]');
		const question = find('[data-undo-question]');
		const status = find('[data-thought-status]');
		const allRows = [...thought.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-change]')];
		const count = (n: number) => `${n} change${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
		let rows = allRows;

		thought.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
			const button = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('button');
			if (!button || !thought.contains(button)) return;
			const { dataset } = button;
			if (dataset.answer) {
				const confirmed = dataset.answer === 'approve';
				rows = allRows.filter((row) => confirmed || row.dataset.comment === undefined);
				allRows.forEach((row) => (row.hidden = !rows.includes(row)));
				actions.hidden = true;
				find('[data-confirm]').classList.remove('is-open');
				outcome.hidden = false;
				outcome.textContent = confirmed ? 'You confirmed this.' : 'You cancelled this.';
				doneText.textContent = confirmed ? 'Posted the comment for Priya on "Refund status emails".' : 'Left the comment out. The sprint move and the reassignment stay.';
				summary.textContent = `Made ${count(rows.length)} in Odin`;
				done.hidden = false;
				status.textContent = confirmed ? 'Priya gets an email about the comment.' : 'No comment was posted, so nobody was emailed.';
				undo.focus({ preventScroll: true });
			} else if (dataset.undo !== undefined) {
				question.textContent = `Undo these ${count(rows.length)}? Anything edited since stays as it is.`;
				undo.hidden = true;
				ask.hidden = false;
				find<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-undo-yes]').focus({ preventScroll: true });
			} else if (dataset.undoNo !== undefined) {
				ask.hidden = true;
				undo.hidden = false;
				undo.focus({ preventScroll: true });
			} else if (dataset.undoYes !== undefined) {
				ask.hidden = true;
				rows.forEach((row) => row.classList.add('is-undone'));
				summary.textContent = `Undid these ${count(rows.length)}`;
				status.textContent = `Undid ${count(rows.length)}.`;
				summary.setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');
				summary.focus({ preventScroll: true });
			}
		});
	}

	// Memory: search and forget, as on the "What the AI remembers" screen.
	const memory = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-memory]');
	if (memory) {
		const input = memory.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-memory-search]')!;
		const rows = [...memory.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-memory-row]')];
		const empty = memory.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-memory-empty]')!;
		const filter = () => {
			const q = input.value.trim().toLowerCase();
			let shown = 0;
			rows.forEach((row) => {
				const match = !q || row.textContent!.toLowerCase().includes(q);
				row.hidden = !match || row.classList.contains('is-gone');
				if (!row.hidden) shown += 1;
			});
			empty.hidden = shown > 0;
		};
		input.addEventListener('input', filter);
		memory.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-hint]').forEach((hint) =>
			hint.addEventListener('click', () => {
				input.value = hint.dataset.hint!;
				filter();
				input.focus();
			}),
		);
		memory.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
			const button = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-forget]');
			if (!button) return;
			const row = button.closest<HTMLElement>('[data-memory-row]')!;
			if (row.classList.contains('is-forgetting')) {
				row.classList.remove('is-forgetting');
				button.textContent = 'Forget';
				return;
			}
			row.classList.add('is-forgetting');
			button.textContent = 'Undo';
			window.setTimeout(() => {
				if (!row.classList.contains('is-forgetting')) return;
				row.classList.add('is-gone');
				filter();
			}, 2600);
		});
	}
</script>

<style>
	.ravens__grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem);
	}
	.raven {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1.25rem;
	}
	.raven header {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.9rem;
	}
	.raven h3 {
		font-size: var(--step-3);
	}
	.raven h3 span {
		margin-left: 0.4em;
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-stretch: 100%;
		font-weight: 400;
		font-size: var(--step-0);
		letter-spacing: 0;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.raven__rune {
		width: 40px;
		height: 40px;
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--gold);
		stroke-width: 3;
		stroke-linecap: square;
	}
	.raven__lede {
		max-width: 52ch;
		color: var(--ink-2);
	}
	.raven__facts {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.4rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
		font-size: var(--step--1);
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.raven__facts li {
		position: relative;
		padding-left: 1rem;
	}
	.raven__facts li::before {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		top: 0.55em;
		width: 6px;
		height: 6px;
		background: var(--line-2);
		transform: rotate(45deg);
	}

	/* Interactive app panels share the real app's look. */
	.thought,
	.memory {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 10px;
		min-height: 470px;
		padding: 16px;
		border-radius: var(--radius-m);
		border: 1px solid var(--line);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-2);
		user-select: text;
	}
	.thought__ask {
		display: flex;
		gap: 9px;
		align-items: center;
	}
	.thought__ask p {
		padding: 8px 12px;
		border-radius: 10px;
		background: var(--a-accent-soft);
	}
	.thought button {
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.thought [hidden] {
		display: none !important;
	}
	.reply {
		display: grid;
		gap: 8px;
	}
	.a-btn--danger {
		background: var(--a-bad);
		border-color: var(--a-bad);
		color: #fff;
	}
	:global(:root[data-theme='dark']) .a-btn--danger {
		color: #07111f;
	}
	.confirm,
	.changes {
		display: grid;
		gap: 8px;
		padding: 10px 12px;
		border-radius: 10px;
		border: 1px solid var(--a-line);
		background: var(--a-surface);
	}
	.confirm.is-open {
		border-color: var(--a-bad);
		border-left-width: 3px;
	}
	.confirm__title {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 6px;
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.confirm__actions,
	.changes__ask {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 6px;
	}
	.changes__ask p {
		flex-basis: 100%;
	}
	.changes__head {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 12px;
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.changes__head [data-changes-summary]:focus {
		outline: none;
	}
	.changes__undo {
		padding: 2px 4px;
		border: 0;
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: none;
		color: var(--a-accent);
		font: inherit;
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.changes__list {
		display: grid;
		gap: 4px;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}
	.changes__list li {
		display: flex;
		gap: 8px;
		align-items: baseline;
	}
	.changes__list li::before {
		content: '\2713';
		color: var(--a-ok);
	}
	.changes__state {
		display: none;
		margin-left: auto;
		color: var(--a-muted);
	}
	.changes__list li:global(.is-undone)::before {
		content: '\21BA';
		color: var(--a-muted);
	}
	.changes__list li:global(.is-undone) span:first-child {
		color: var(--a-muted);
	}
	.changes__list li:global(.is-undone) .changes__state {
		display: inline;
	}
	.thought__status {
		margin-top: auto;
	}

	.memory__search {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 8px;
		padding: 8px 12px;
		border-radius: 9px;
		border: 1px solid var(--a-line-2);
		background: var(--a-surface);
		color: var(--a-muted);
	}
	.memory__search input {
		flex: 1;
		border: 0;
		outline: 0;
		background: transparent;
		font: inherit;
		color: var(--a-ink);
	}
	.memory__search:focus-within {
		border-color: var(--a-accent);
		box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--a-accent-soft);
	}
	.memory__hints {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 6px;
		color: var(--a-muted);
	}
	.memory__hints button {
		padding: 1px 8px;
		border: 1px dashed var(--a-line-2);
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: transparent;
		font-size: 11px;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.memories {
		display: grid;
		gap: 6px;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}
	.memory-row {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 74px minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
		gap: 10px;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 8px 10px;
		border-radius: 9px;
		background: var(--a-surface);
		border: 1px solid var(--a-line);
		transition: opacity 0.4s ease, filter 0.4s ease;
	}
	.memory-row .a-chip {
		justify-self: start;
	}
	.memory-row[hidden] {
		display: none;
	}
	.memory-row:global(.is-forgetting) p {
		text-decoration: line-through;
		opacity: 0.5;
	}
	.forget {
		cursor: pointer;
	}

	@media (max-width: 960px) {
		.ravens__grid {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
	}
	@media (max-width: 560px) {
		.memory-row {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
		}
		.memory-row .a-chip {
			grid-column: 1 / -1;
		}
	}
</style>
